    "about": {
      "kicker": "01 · About the school",
      "title": "Serving Arutla and its neighbouring villages",
      "paragraphs": [
        "ZPHS Arutla offers Classes VI to X, preparing students for the SSC examinations of the Board of Secondary Education, Telangana. Under PM SHRI the school is being developed as a model for the mandal — with activity-based learning, green campus practices and stronger links to the community.",
        "Since November 2024 the school has been part of Telangana Public School (TPS) Arutla, the State's first demonstration campus that brings four government schools, two Anganwadi centres and two hostels together as one integrated public school from Pre-Primary to Class 12.",
        "Education is free. Textbooks, uniforms, breakfast, a hot mid-day meal and evening snacks are provided to every student."
      ],
      "link": { "label": "History, staff and disclosures →", "href": "/about" }
    },
